  - AC.FBMT1.ENCC.1 — Worker emits `context:` block with EXACTLY
    the four named fields (`triggering_msg_id`, `active_task_id`,
    `cwd`, `active_files`) — no more, no less. Structurally
    enforces TG 11805 schema-minimal directive.
  - AC.FBMT1.ENCC.2 — Fields carry values when input has them;
    `null` (still present in YAML) when absent.
  - AC.FBMT1.ENCC.3 — `active_files` is a list; non-list input
    is a schema-validation error.
  - AC.FBMT1.ENCC.4 — Pre-amendment memory files (no `context:`)
    still parse + retrieve cleanly (backwards-compat).
  - AC.FBMT1.FCS.1 — Post-seal hook reads sealed plan-doc, scans
    FIDRAFT for slug-overlap above confidence threshold, emits
    surfacing payload (NOT a file edit).
  - AC.FBMT1.FCS.2 — Hook never writes FIDRAFT (SHA + mtime
    unchanged after hook fires).
  - AC.FBMT1.FCS.3 — Zero false-positive surfacing when no
    FIDRAFT entry matches above threshold.
  - AC.FBMT1.FCS.4 — `--skip-fidraft-cleanup` (or equivalent
    flag) bypasses the hook for emergency seals.
  - AC.FBMT1.APS.1 — Plan-doc + manifest at `docs/plans/sealed/`
    after `loam amend seal`; seal commit includes the rename.
  - AC.FBMT1.APS.2 — Plan-doc content byte-identical post-move;
    internal cross-references functional.
  - AC.FBMT1.APS.3 — One-shot retroactive sweep moves
    sealed-but-not-archived plan-docs; in-flight plans stay in
